WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.622
Authorization caches reduce latency and
dependency load,

2
00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:07.324
but a cached value is evidence only under
a defined freshness policy.

3
00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:09.714
A cache miss, parse failure, expired
entry,

4
00:00:09.794 --> 00:00:11.980
or cache outage does not establish allow.

5
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.181
Replacing any of those states with a
global default permit creates a fail-open

6
00:00:16.261 --> 00:00:16.823
fallback.

7
00:00:16.903 --> 00:00:21.150
The application must either obtain a
trustworthy decision or stop the protected

8
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:21.854
operation.

9
00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.995
Treat cache contents as security data:

10
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:28.758
validate their structure and prevent
untrusted writers from manufacturing decisions.

11
00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:32.148
Cache keys should bind the subject,
tenant, resource, action,

12
00:00:32.228 --> 00:00:36.536
relevant attributes, and policy version
closely enough to prevent reuse across a

13
00:00:36.616 --> 00:00:37.740
different decision.

14
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.193
Positive entries need explicit expiration,

15
00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:44.082
and sensitive systems may require
revocation events, short lifetimes,

16
00:00:44.162 --> 00:00:46.598
or fresh evaluation for high-impact
actions.

17
00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:48.988
Negative caching can reduce repeated work,

18
00:00:49.068 --> 00:00:53.564
but its lifetime also affects how quickly
a newly granted permission becomes usable.

19
00:00:53.644 --> 00:00:56.642
Both directions involve correctness and
availability.

20
00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.469
Stale authorization is not universally
forbidden,

21
00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:01.672
but it must be an explicit risk decision.

22
00:01:01.752 --> 00:01:05.499
A limited stale window may be acceptable
for a low-risk read when policy

23
00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:07.327
infrastructure is unavailable.

24
00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:11.841
The same choice may be unacceptable for
financial changes, administrator actions,

25
00:01:11.921 --> 00:01:14.856
or environments with strict revocation
requirements.

26
00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:17.871
Bound the window, document which
operations permit it,

27
00:01:17.951 --> 00:01:22.197
record when stale evidence was used, and
never allow an indefinite stale permit.

28
00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:26.773
Distinguish last-known-good configuration
from a last-known allow for one subject

29
00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.602
and resource.

30
00:01:27.682 --> 00:01:32.178
Stable signed policy configuration may let
an in-process evaluator continue making

31
00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.195
fresh decisions.

32
00:01:33.275 --> 00:01:37.396
A cached permit can preserve privilege
after membership or ownership has been

33
00:01:37.476 --> 00:01:37.976
revoked.

34
00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:41.053
Ask what evidence still justifies this
exact action now.

35
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:45.754
Improve authorization-service replication,
local evaluation, cache availability,

36
00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:49.893
and operational recovery without quietly
redefining dependency failure as

37
00:01:49.973 --> 00:01:50.660
permission.
